      <section class="section-pad" id="purpose" aria-labelledby="purpose-title">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow section-label"><span>01 /</span> Purpose &amp; values</p>
              <h2 id="purpose-title">Make knowledge<br />work in practice.</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="about-copy">
              <p>
                Our purpose is to help people turn scientific knowledge and technical
                ideas into useful, lasting tools.
              </p>
              <p>
                Our mission is to build reliable software and data solutions with
                research teams, businesses, and open-source communities, sharing
                the knowledge they need to use and maintain them.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="engagement-grid">
            <article>
              <span class="eyebrow">[ 01 ] Evidence</span>
              <h3>Scientific rigor</h3>
              <p>Question assumptions, test our work, and make methods and limitations clear.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span class="eyebrow">[ 02 ] Openness</span>
              <h3>Open collaboration</h3>
              <p>Share reusable work when project agreements allow, communicate openly, and credit contributions.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span class="eyebrow">[ 03 ] Longevity</span>
              <h3>Sustainable engineering</h3>
              <p>Favor maintainable solutions, useful documentation, and choices that fit the team’s resources.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span class="eyebrow">[ 04 ] People</span>
              <h3>Inclusion &amp; respect</h3>
              <p>Welcome different perspectives and consider accessibility in how we work and what we build.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span class="eyebrow">[ 05 ] Care</span>
              <h3>Responsible technology</h3>
              <p>Handle data with care and consider privacy, risks, and the effects of software and AI on people.</p>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span class="eyebrow">[ 06 ] Learning</span>
              <h3>Shared capability</h3>
              <p>Learn together and transfer knowledge so collaborators can understand, use, and extend the work.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
          <div class="section-note">
            <span class="note-symbol" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
            <p>Our vision is a future where research and technology are easier to understand, reuse, and build on.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section
        class="team-journey section-pad"
        id="selected-work"
        aria-labelledby="journey-title"
      >
        <div class="container section-grid">
          <div class="section-intro">
            <p class="eyebrow section-label">
              <span>02 /</span> Our story
            </p>
            <h2 id="journey-title"><span id="our-story"></span>Real projects.<br />Lasting connections.</h2>
            <p>
              Research collaborations and support for OSL’s wider community
              shaped our team before SciStitch became independent.
            </p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/projects/">Explore our contributions <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          </div>
          <ol class="story-timeline" role="list">
            <li>
              <span class="eyebrow story-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
              <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">Supporting open research</p>
                <h3>Infodengue</h3>
                <p>
              An early OSL team supported Infodengue, an open-source project monitoring
              mosquito-borne diseases in Brazil. Some contributors were later contracted
              directly by the project.
            </p>

                <div class="inline-links">
                  <a href="https://info.dengue.mat.br/"
                    >Explore Infodengue <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                  >
                  <a href="https://info.dengue.mat.br/informacoes/"
                    >About the project <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                  >
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="eyebrow story-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
              <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">Building another team</p>
                <h3>LiteRev</h3>
                <p>
              OSL then formed another team to work on LiteRev, a tool for finding and
              reviewing scientific literature.
            </p>
                <p>
              LiteRev is connected to The GRAPH Network (Global Research and Analyses for
              Public Health) and research at the University of Geneva (UNIGE).
            </p>
                <div class="inline-links">
                  <a href="https://literev.unige.ch/"
                    >Explore LiteRev <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                  >
                  <a href="https://thegraphnetwork.org/"
                    >The GRAPH Network <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                  >
                  <a
                    href="https://www.unige.ch/medecine/isg/research/infectious-diseases-and-mathematical-modelling-professor-olivia-keiser/group-members/erol-orel"
                    >LiteRev at UNIGE <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                  >
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="eyebrow story-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
              <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">Supporting the wider community</p>
                <h3>OSL Incubator &amp; initiatives</h3>
                <p>
                  Alongside these research collaborations, we supported the OSL
                  Incubator Program through development and maintenance of
                  open-source tools, including Makim, Sugar, and PyMedX.
                </p>
                <p>
                  We also created and maintained OSL’s technical infrastructure,
                  from bots and continuous integration to websites, plugins, and
                  DevOps workflows. Our support extended to other OSL initiatives
                  and collaborations with some of its partners.
                </p>
                <div class="inline-links">
                  <a href="https://opensciencelabs.org/projects/incubation/"
                    >OSL Incubator Program <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                  >
                  <a href="/projects/#osl-projects"
                    >Our OSL contributions <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                  >
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="eyebrow story-index" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
              <div>
                <p class="eyebrow">Becoming independent</p>
                <h3>SciStitch</h3>
                <p>
                  This shared experience became the foundation for SciStitch,
                  an independent consulting organization formed by the research
                  software engineering team.
            </p>
                <p>
                  OSL can call on SciStitch for external consulting and
                  development requests.
            </p>
                <div class="inline-links">
                  <a href="/partnership/"
                    >Our partnership with OSL
                    <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                  >
                  <a href="/services/"
                    >How we can help <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
                  >
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </section>

